      "claim": "L1/L2 records report low, poor, or <1% oral bioavailability for multiple tetracyclic terpenoid/steroid and diterpenoid contexts relevant to the query: andrographolide poor in humans and 0.3% (C13, C18), docetaxel low absolute F in humans and 0.315% in rats (C08, C23), withaferin A poor in humans and ~9% in mice (C10, C25), fluticasone <1% (C07, C15, C28), mometasone <1%/negligible (C04, C24), anecortave desacetate low/very low (C05, C27, C29), Rg3 low/2.63% (C14, C26), rifaximin <0.4% (C01, C17), and sitostanol 0.04% (C03). These support F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C03","C04","C05","C07","C08","C10","C13","C14","C15","C17","C18","C23","C24","C25","C26","C27","C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records show very low plasma exposure after oral dosing in humans: abiraterone acetate Cmax 54.67 pg/mL and AUCt/AUCinf about 460/386 pg·h/mL (C36, C39, C34, C41, C37); pachymic acid Cmax 36.3–91.0 pg/mL after 2.5–7.5 g rikkunshito (C32, C33, C30, C31, C35, C38, C40). These are consistent with poor oral absorption/exposure for structurally related terpenoid acids/prodrugs, though they lack IV comparators and are not direct F values.",
      "card_ids": ["C30","C31","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36","C37","C38","C39","C40","C41"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The single high absolute F for withaferin A in rats (87%, C16) is species- and formulation-specific and conflicts with the human poor outcome (C10); it does not provide affirmative evidence for F >= 20% in the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C16","C10"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C30","C31","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36","C37","C38","C39","C40","C41"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "L3 exposure records lack IV comparators and dose-normalized AUC, so very low pg/mL Cmax/AUC is indirect rather than direct F evidence.",
    "Several L3 cards are duplicate records of the same measurements (e.g., C36/C39, C34/C41, C30/C35/C38, C31/C40, C32/C33), so they are not independent.",
    "Structural similarity to low-bioavailability contexts is qualitative; exact scaffold and functional-group match is not established.",
    "Species and formulation differences, such as withaferin A 87% in rats versus poor in humans, create uncertainty in transfer.",
    "No query-specific absorption, permeability, or first-pass metabolism data are available."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains low and is strengthened by L3 oral exposure records showing very low pg/mL Cmax/AUC for abiraterone acetate and pachymic acid after oral dosing in humans, consistent with the low/poor F evidence from L1/L2 terpenoid/steroid contexts. No affirmative evidence supports F >= 20%; the single high rat withaferin A value is species/formulation-specific."
}

